V3.1.1
      added support for detecting all functions that overrride other commands.
      And made alias override detection more robust.

V3.0.0
      Now we have this 1200+ line mess in BASH
      Why did I do this?

V2.0.0  
      A small function using fc similar to this:
      h() {
          last_cmd=$(fc -ln -1 | awk '{print $1}')
          # Run the last command with --help appended
          eval "$last_cmd --help"
      }

V1.0.0
      Simply an alias
      alias h='eval "$(history -p \!\! | awk '\''{print $1}'\'')" --help'
